# Prompt & Token Optimization Rule

- **Auto-Infer Rough & Shorthand Input**: When user writes short/informal Marathi/Hinglish (e.g. "he fix kr", "EmailSenderModel soft delete fix"):
  - Silently identify target files from open tabs, cursor position, or `PROJECT_MAP.md`.
  - When user pastes a raw error/trace, jump straight to the fix without repeating the error.
  - Apply CI4 standards, CSRF, escaping, and activity logging without asking questions.
  - Never repeat back the prompt or explain what you are about to do.
- **Minimum Token Protocol**:
  - Direct execution, zero preamble/pleasantries.
  - No unsolicited explanations: code execution only; never explain how/why unless user explicitly asks "explain" or "kasa kela sang".
  - Surgical edits only via `replace_file_content`. No full-file rewrites.
  - Final response max 1-3 lines with clickable file links. Do not dump duplicate code in chat.
